    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d319">

                <pb facs="0595" n="499" sameAs="frus:frus1926v02/pg499"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.60 p 31/36: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Latvia</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Coleman</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-01-28T20:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 28,
                                1926—8 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>7. Your 10, January 28, 1 p.m. Department cannot approve suggested substitution
                    for “Russia” which appears in <hi rendition="#italic">modi vivendi</hi> with
                        Esthonia<anchor n="23" xml:id="d319-f1"/> and Lithuania.<anchor n="24"
                        xml:id="d319-f2"/> Department approves insertion of statement that the
                    agreement will be effective upon ratification by Latvian Parliament and notice
                    to that effect.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
